          "facts": {
            "report_text": "CHEST X-RAY REPORT FINDINGS: frontal and lateral views of the chest were obtained. the right internal jugular central venous catheter is seen terminating in the distal svc. the enteric tube is seen coursing below the level of the diaphragm and out of the field of view. extensive bilateral pulmonary opacities persist. there is also evidence of extensive subcutaneous emphysema. the cardiac silhouette is top normal. the mediastinal contours are stable. IMPRESSION: 1. right internal jugular central line has its tip in the distal svc. a nasogastric tube is seen coursing below the diaphragm with the tip not identified. there continues to be diffuse bilateral airspace process which is not significantly changed and could reflect pulmonary edema, ards, pulmonary hemorrhage or a diffuse infectious process. clinical correlation is advised. overall, cardiac and mediastinal contours are likely stable given differences in patient positioning. no pneumothorax is seen, although the sensitivity to detect pneumothorax is diminished given supine technique."
